# Lumbering Laundry: "{2}: Until end of turn, you may look at face-down creatures you don't control any time" (CR 611.2a,
# 708.5) - creatures only. Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Laundry and a Mox. Turn 2 Bot2 casts Vengeful Creeper and Basilica Stalker
# face down for their disguise costs. Turn 3 Bot1 casts Imprisoned in the Moon on the face-down Creeper, paying its ward {2}:
# it is now a colorless land and no creature (CR 205.1b), still face down. Bot1 then pays {2} for the Laundry's ability and
# knows the Stalker, but not the face-down land.

